## Key Architectural Decisions

- **One plugin per metric, declaring everything.** `MetricDescriptor` names the fields, their kinds, the unit, and which field becomes `value`; `bounds()` names the threshold keys; `actions()` names what the metric can be told to do. `GET /contracts` and `POST /ingest` are driven by the same declaration, so the catalog and the validator cannot drift.
- **Ports for every technology.** The kernel holds `Arc<dyn ReadingStore>`, not a `PgPool`. The whole kernel is unit-tested against in-memory fakes with no database in sight.
- **Persist before publish.** A reading reaches Postgres before it reaches Redis, so no consumer sees an event that is not yet queryable. Publishing is fire-and-forget: a broker failure is logged and never fails an ingest that already landed.
- **Threshold scope is a column, not a nesting depth.** `room_id NULL` means building-level; a room-level row wins during resolution. Room thresholds cannot be silently dropped.
- **Room thresholds are set in one request, not one per room.** `PATCH /thresholds/{sensorType}/buildings/{id}/rooms` takes a map of room id to bounds. Registering a building sets a threshold for every room at once, and one request per room made that both the bulk of the round trips — each paying its own edge auth — and partially appliable. Every patch is validated before any is written, so a rejected bound stores nothing. The writes are still one upsert per room: the store has no transactional bulk write, and a mid-write failure is rare and idempotent to retry.
- **Device vocabulary lives behind one port.** `ActionDispatch` takes a `Command` in our own vocabulary; URLs, methods and field names exist only in the dispatch adapter. See [Sensor Actions & the Device ACL](../design/sensor-actions.qd).
- **Authorization asks the owner.** Building-to-domain lookups go to digital-twin over its existing endpoint rather than into a local copy of someone else's data; a failed lookup denies.

---

## Integration

- Owns `telemetry-db` (Postgres + TimescaleDB); no other service reads it. Retention and rollup policy in [Telemetry Storage & Retention](../design/telemetry-storage.qd).
- Publishes every accepted reading to Redis `telemetry:raw`, and every threshold breach to the Kafka `alerts` topic keyed `buildingId:roomId`, with no reference to whichever service consumes them. Breaches are enqueued, never awaited (`send_result`), so a broker outage cannot stall `/telemetry/ingest`.
- Receives a threshold baseline from digital-twin: over Kafka for a new building's registration, over REST (`PUT /thresholds/buildings/:id`) for every later edit. Both are driving adapters over the **same** registration use case.
- Exposes a self-describing metric catalog to dashboard at `GET /contracts`, now including each metric's available actions.
- Scraped at `/metrics`. See [Observability](observability.qd).

For the request lifecycle, the plugin template, the extension guide, and the API, see the [Telemetry Service](../services/telemetry.qd) internals page.
